{{ The JS function the loader builds a module's imports with: the runtime, its JS functions and code table, the string constants, and a JS version of every `wasm:js-string` builtin warp imports, which a browser without the builtins (Safari before 26.2, for one) takes in their place. A missing one there fails instantiation. }}
internal.javascript.supportJS.buildImportsJS : Text
internal.javascript.supportJS.buildImportsJS =
  """
  (rt) => ({
    runtime: rt,
    js: rt.js,
    code: rt.code.terms,
    '': new Proxy({}, { get: (_, k) => k }),
    'wasm:js-string': {
      equals: (a, b) => a === b,
      compare: (a, b) => a === b ? 0 : a < b ? -1 : 1,
      concat: (a, b) => a + b,
      length: (s) => s.length,
      charCodeAt: (s, i) => s.charCodeAt(i >>> 0),
      codePointAt: (s, i) => s.codePointAt(i >>> 0),
      substring: (s, start, end) => (start >>>= 0) > (end >>>= 0) ? '' : s.substring(start, end),
      fromCodePoint: (c) => String.fromCodePoint(c >>> 0),
    },
  })
  """

ReleaseNotes : Doc
ReleaseNotes =
  {{
  * Introduced a notion of incremental builds, enabling {type IO}-based builds
    to produce lightweight WebAssembly modules containing only terms that
    weren't already present in previous build output. See {incremental} and
    {loadCompiledTerms} for details.
  * 2026-10-31: In a browser without the `wasm:js-string` builtins (Safari
    before 26.2, for one), the loader supplies every builtin warp imports:
    `length`, `charCodeAt`, `codePointAt`, `substring` and `fromCodePoint`
    as well as `equals`, `compare` and `concat`. Before, such a browser
    could not instantiate a module that imported one of the five.
  * 2026-10-30: JS builtins can take their arguments unboxed and box their
    results in wasm ({internal.Replacement.jsUnboxed}), so the JS function
    makes no calls back into wasm. The `JSValue` interop functions
    (`invoke*`, `getProperty`, `setProperty*`, `callback1_`), `Nat.toText`
    and `Text.indexOf` use it. A UI creating 1,000 table rows crossed the
    wasm–JS boundary 197,231 times before and 32,046 after.
  * 2026-10-30: `Universal.==` compares a plain function with a closure by
    id in wasm instead of in JS.
  * 2026-10-30: `Universal.compare`, `Universal.==` and the builtins with a
    `Boolean` result return shared result boxes
    ({internal.Replacement.sharedValues}) instead of allocating one per call.
  * 2026-10-30: `Text.size`, `Text.take` and `Text.drop` run in wasm over the
    `wasm:js-string` builtins (`length`, `substring`), with no call into JS.
  * 2026-10-30: `Char.toText`, `Char.toNat`, `Char.fromNat`, `Text.uncons` and
    `Text.unsnoc` also run in wasm over `wasm:js-string`.
  * 2026-10-30: `Text.repeat` and `Text.reverse` run in wasm too.
  }}
